    "title": "Putin Invites Trump to Moscow in May: Key Details Revealed",
    "text": "Russian President⁣ Vladimir Putin has invited ⁢the leaders of the Commonwealth of autonomous States ( CIS ) ‌nations to Moscow to celebrate the 80th‌ anniversary of Victory in the Great Patriotic War , which marks the defeat of Nazi Germany and the‍ end ‍of World War II on the Eastern Front.⁢ This event is traditionally commemorated with a large military parade in Red Square , Moscow.\nIn 2023 , the Moscow Victory Day Parade was held on 9 May, but it was scaled down due to the ongoing Russian ‍invasion of Ukraine and other geopolitical tensions. ​Despite these circumstances, several leaders from former Soviet republics⁢ were expected to ‍attend, including Belarus President Alexander Lukashenko.\nAdditionally, it​ was reported‌ that China’s President Xi Jinping agreed to visit Moscow on the same day, ‍highlighting⁤ the significance⁣ of the ⁤event. Kremlin spokesman ‍Dmitry Peskov ​emphasized the importance of the day, ⁢stating that it symbolizes the victory over fascism and is ​particularly relevant in the current global context.",
